{"type":"message","id":"3808ed3e","parentId":"b795e3f6","timestamp":"2026-04-22T11:51:07.110Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[media attached: 2 files]\n[media attached 1/2: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/p003_genomic_profile---9983dc02-a97c-4599-9ef3-155e1ec7b766.json (application/json) | /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/p003_genomic_profile---9983dc02-a97c-4599-9ef3-155e1ec7b766.json]\n[media attached 2/2: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/p003_genomic_profile---8084f72b-dfbd-4ad4-ab1b-e88a3e335ddd.pdf (application/pdf) | /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/p003_genomic_profile---8084f72b-dfbd-4ad4-ab1b-e88a3e335ddd.pdf]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Avoid absolute paths (MEDIA:/...) and ~ paths - they are blocked for security. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"41\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"sender\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-04-22 11:51 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Matteo Cicalese (495506013)\",\n  \"id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"name\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"username\": \"CicaMatt\"\n}\n```\n\n[Telegram Matteo Cicalese (@CicaMatt) id:495506013 +19s Wed 2026-04-22 11:51 UTC] <media:document>\n\n<file name=\"p003_genomic_profile---9983dc02-a97c-4599-9ef3-155e1ec7b766.json\" mime=\"application/json\">\n\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c25429fb43f5eea\">>>\nSource: External\n---\n{\n \"patient_id\": \"P-003\",\n \"profiling_date\": \"2023-02-14\",\n \"platform\": \"clinical_exome_panel\",\n \"genetic_variants\": [\n {\n \"gene\": \"ACE\",\n \"variant_id\": \"rs4646994\",\n \"zygosity\": \"homozygous\",\n \"clinical_significance\": \"risk_factor\",\n \"associated_condition\": \"hypertension, CKD progression\",\n \"effect\": \"D allele homozygous \\u2014 higher ACE activity, associated with faster CKD progression and LVH\",\n \"evidence_level\": \"II\"\n },\n {\n \"gene\": \"AGT\",\n \"variant_id\": \"rs699\",\n \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\",\n \"clinical_significance\": \"likely_pathogenic\",\n \"associated_condition\": \"essential hypertension\",\n \"effect\": \"M235T variant \\u2014 increased angiotensinogen levels, elevated BP risk\",\n \"evidence_level\": \"II\"\n },\n {\n \"gene\": \"SCN5A\",\n \"variant_id\": \"rs1805124\",\n \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\",\n \"clinical_significance\": \"VUS\",\n \"associated_condition\": \"atrial fibrillation predisposition\",\n \"effect\": \"Sodium channel variant, borderline reduced conduction velocity\",\n \"evidence_level\": \"III\"\n },\n {\n \"gene\": \"APOL1\",\n \"variant_id\": \"rs73885319\",\n \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\",\n \"clinical_significance\": \"risk_factor\",\n \"associated_condition\": \"CKD, focal segmental glomerulosclerosis\",\n \"effect\": \"G1 variant carrier \\u2014 moderate increased CKD risk\",\n \"evidence_level\": \"II\"\n },\n {\n \"gene\": \"CYP2C9\",\n \"variant_id\": \"rs1799853\",\n \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\",\n \"clinical_significance\": \"pharmacogenomic\",\n \"associated_condition\": \"anticoagulant metabolism\",\n \"effect\": \"*2 allele \\u2014 intermediate metaboliser, dose adjustment needed for warfarin\",\n \"evidence_level\": \"I\"\n },\n {\n \"gene\": \"NPHS2\",\n \"variant_id\": \"rs3829795\",\n \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\",\n \"clinical_significance\": \"VUS\",\n \"associated_condition\": \"proteinuria, podocyte dysfunction\",\n \"effect\": \"Podocin variant contributing to persistent proteinuria\",\n \"evidence_level\": \"III\"\n }\n ],\n \"polygenic_risk_scores\": {\n \"hypertension_prs\": {\n \"score\": 2.34,\n \"percentile\": 88,\n \"interpretation\": \"High genetic risk for essential hypertension. Score indicates 2.8-fold increased risk compared to population median.\"\n },\n \"ckd_progression_prs\": {\n \"score\": 1.89,\n \"percentile\": 79,\n \"interpretation\": \"Elevated genetic risk for CKD progression. Consistent with advanced stage 4 CKD presentation.\"\n },\n \"atrial_fibrillation_prs\": {\n \"score\": 1.67,\n \"percentile\": 73,\n \"interpretation\": \"Moderately elevated genetic susceptibility to atrial fibrillation, particularly in context of structural heart disease.\"\n }\n },\n \"pharmacogenomics\": {\n \"ACE_inhibitor_response\": \"Normal response expected. ACE DD genotype may require higher doses for optimal BP control.\",\n \"anticoagulant_metabolism\": \"CYP2C9*2 carrier - reduce initial warfarin dose by 25-30%. Monitor INR closely during initiation.\",\n \"statin_metabolism\": \"Normal metabolism expected. Standard dosing appropriate.\",\n \"diuretic_response\": \"Good response to thiazide-type diuretics predicted based on genetic profile.\"\n },\n \"dna_fragments\": [\n {\n \"fragment_id\": \"FRAG-P003-001\",\n \"gene_region\": \"ACE intron 16\",\n \"sequence_excerpt\": \"CTGGAGACCACTCCCATCCTTTCT\",\n \"length_bp\": 287,\n \"mutation_sites\": [\n \"rs4646994 deletion polymorphism at position 144\"\n ]\n },\n {\n \"fragment_id\": \"FRAG-P003-002\",\n \"gene_region\": \"AGT exon 2\",\n \"sequence_excerpt\": \"ATGCAGCGCATCCTGGTCATC\",\n \"length_bp\": 198,\n \"mutation_sites\": [\n \"rs699 C>T at position 89\"\n ]\n },\n {\n \"fragment_id\": \"FRAG-P003-003\",\n \"gene_region\": \"SCN5A exon 28\",\n \"sequence_excerpt\": \"GAGCTGGTGGCCTTTGTGAAC\",\n \"length_bp\": 312,\n \"mutation_sites\": [\n \"heterozygous missense at position 156\"\n ]\n }\n ],\n \"family_history_genetic_notes\": \"Father with CAD and hypertension. Paternal uncle with CKD. Pattern consistent with polygenic cardiovascular-renal risk inheritance.\",\n \"clinical_summary\": \"58-year-old South Asian male with advanced CKD stage 4, hypertension, and atrial fibrillation showing genetic predisposition through multiple cardiovascular-renal risk variants. ACE DD genotype and AGT M235T variant contribute to hypertension severity. APOL1 G1 carrier status partially explains CKD progression. SCN5A variant provides genetic context for atrial fibrillation. CYP2C9*2 carrier status requires warfarin dose adjustment. High polygenic risk scores support aggressive cardiovascular risk management and close monitoring of CKD progression.\"\n}\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c25429fb43f5eea\">>>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"p003_genomic_profile---8084f72b-dfbd-4ad4-ab1b-e88a3e335ddd.pdf\" mime=\"application/pdf\">\n\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20bfef42c17a9749\">>>\nSource: External\n---\nGenomic Profile Report { \"patient_id\": \"P-003\", \"profiling_date\": \"2023-02-14\", \"platform\": \"clinical_exome_panel\", \"genetic_variants\": [ { \"gene\": \"ACE\", \"variant_id\": \"rs4646994\", \"zygosity\": \"homozygous\", \"clinical_significance\": \"risk_factor\", \"associated_condition\": \"hypertension, CKD progression\", \"effect\": \"D allele homozygous \\u2014 higher ACE activity, associated with faster CKD progressi \"evidence_level\": \"II\" }, { \"gene\": \"AGT\", \"variant_id\": \"rs699\", \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\", \"clinical_significance\": \"likely_pathogenic\", \"associated_condition\": \"essential hypertension\", \"effect\": \"M235T variant \\u2014 increased angiotensinogen levels, elevated BP risk\", \"evidence_level\": \"II\" }, { \"gene\": \"SCN5A\", \"variant_id\": \"rs1805124\", \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\", \"clinical_significance\": \"VUS\", \"associated_condition\": \"atrial fibrillation predisposition\", \"effect\": \"Sodium channel variant, borderline reduced conduction velocity\", \"evidence_level\": \"III\" }, { \"gene\": \"APOL1\", \"variant_id\": \"rs73885319\", \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\", \"clinical_significance\": \"risk_factor\", \"associated_condition\": \"CKD, focal segmental glomerulosclerosis\", \"effect\": \"G1 variant carrier \\u2014 moderate increased CKD risk\", \"evidence_level\": \"II\" }, { \"gene\": \"CYP2C9\", \"variant_id\": \"rs1799853\", \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\", \"clinical_significance\": \"pharmacogenomic\", \"associated_condition\": \"anticoagulant metabolism\", \"effect\": \"*2 allele \\u2014 intermediate metaboliser, dose adjustment needed for warfarin\", \"evidence_level\": \"I\" }, { \"gene\": \"NPHS2\", \"variant_id\": \"rs3829795\", \"zygosity\": \"heterozygous\", \"clinical_significance\": \"VUS\", \"associated_condition\": \"proteinuria, podocyte dysfunction\", \"effect\": \"Podocin variant contributing to persistent proteinuria\", \"evidence_level\": \"III\" } ], \"polygenic_risk_scores\": { \"hypertension_prs\": { \"score\": 2.34, \"percentile\": 88, \"interpretation\": \"High genetic risk for essential hypertension. Score indicates 2.8-fold incre }, \"ckd_progression_prs\": { \"score\": 1.89, \"percentile\": 79, \"interpretation\": \"Elevated genetic risk for CKD progression. Consistent with advanced stage 4 }, \"atrial_fibrillation_prs\": { \"score\": 1.67,\n\n\"percentile\": 73, \"interpretation\": \"Moderately elevated genetic susceptibility to atrial fibrillation, particula } }, \"pharmacogenomics\": { \"ACE_inhibitor_response\": \"Normal response expected. ACE DD genotype may require higher doses for \"anticoagulant_metabolism\": \"CYP2C9*2 carrier - reduce initial warfarin dose by 25-30%. Monitor I \"statin_metabolism\": \"Normal metabolism expected. Standard dosing appropriate.\", \"diuretic_response\": \"Good response to thiazide-type diuretics predicted based on genetic profile }, \"dna_fragments\": [ { \"fragment_id\": \"FRAG-P003-001\", \"gene_region\": \"ACE intron 16\", \"sequence_excerpt\": \"CTGGAGACCACTCCCATCCTTTCT\", \"length_bp\": 287, \"mutation_sites\": [ \"rs4646994 deletion polymorphism at position 144\" ] }, { \"fragment_id\": \"FRAG-P003-002\", \"gene_region\": \"AGT exon 2\", \"sequence_excerpt\": \"ATGCAGCGCATCCTGGTCATC\", \"length_bp\": 198, \"mutation_sites\": [ \"rs699 C>T at position 89\" ] }, { \"fragment_id\": \"FRAG-P003-003\", \"gene_region\": \"SCN5A exon 28\", \"sequence_excerpt\": \"GAGCTGGTGGCCTTTGTGAAC\", \"length_bp\": 312, \"mutation_sites\": [ \"heterozygous missense at position 156\" ] } ], \"family_history_genetic_notes\": \"Father with CAD and hypertension. Paternal uncle with CKD. Pattern \"clinical_summary\": \"58-year-old South Asian male with advanced CKD stage 4, hypertension, and atri }\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20bfef42c17a9749\">>>\n</file>"}],"timestamp":1776858667108}}
