{"type":"message","id":"c4511d7a","parentId":"bf4a0485","timestamp":"2026-04-22T11:52:49.100Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommended questions**\nUnderstood. Dizziness and reduced appetite can still happen with stress, poor sleep, low mood, dehydration, blood pressure problems, worsening kidney disease, or medication effects, so I want one more key detail.\n\n**(4/4)**\nHave you checked your blood pressure, heart rate, blood sugar, or weight recently, and have there been any medication changes or missed doses over the past month?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0fc6579adecff2a70169e8b68c32d08191aa3ac0beb3b137e3\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":225,"output":89,"cacheRead":30080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30394,"cost":{"input":0.0005625000000000001,"output":0.001335,"cacheRead":0.00752,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0094175}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776858763017,"responseId":"resp_0fc6579adecff2a70169e8b68b4fc88191b9cf551635d612f6"}}
