ight not need exact computations after all. Instead, I could spawn a subagent while keeping the context in mind. It's about ensuring I utilize resources effectively and approach the task smartly without overcomplicating things. I’ll just have to keep this in check as I move forward!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_BQIRaias0vn1hbkiCfutDAK4|fc_0fc6579adecff2a70169e8b70dad648191b52bb8172994b6e7","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"runtime":"subagent","mode":"run","label":"doctor-agent-consult","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent-2","timeoutSeconds":120,"task":"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent, providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. Review this patient case and provide a concise patient-facing assessment in clean Telegram-friendly markdown. Keep it preliminary, not definitive. Do not recommend seeing a physical doctor; you may recommend urgent evaluation if red flags are present.\n\nPatient context from Patient KLM / uploaded DNA for P-003:\n- 58-year-old South Asian male\n- Background conditions in record: CKD progressed to stage 4 by 2025, hypertension, persistent atrial fibrillation, diabetes, obesity, anemia of CKD, cardiorenal syndrome type 4\n- Prior symptoms/history: fatigue, ankle/leg swelling, exertional shortness of breath, palpitations\n- July 2025 findings include eGFR about 25, anemia, AF, echocardiogram EF 45% with diastolic dysfunction\n- Genomics: increased inherited risk related to hypertension, CKD progression, and atrial fibrillation susceptibility; pharmacogenomic note for warfarin metabolism\n\nCurrent user-reported symptoms:\n- 1 month of constant and worsening poor sleep, very low mood, headaches, fatigue\n- Also dizziness, reduced appetite, and unintentional weight loss\n- No med changes reported\n- User says stress from work and family concerns is severe and affecting health\n- No chest pain/tightness, palpitations, worsening shortness of breath, fainting, leg swelling, or self-harm thoughts r