{"type":"message","id":"d9785c37","parentId":"d1979e9c","timestamp":"2026-04-22T13:08:46.657Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Retry result**\nI retried the skin analysis, and this time the pipeline returned a usable result.\n\n**Skin cancer class**\nBenign nevus\n\n**Confidence**\n0.9984\n\n**Image Analyzer prediction**\nnv\n\n**Interpretation**\nThe structured output favors a **benign nevus**, which is a reassuring result. At the same time, I want to keep this careful, because the visible morphology still showed **some asymmetry, irregular borders, and color variation**, so this should be treated as a **preliminary signal**, not a confirmed diagnosis.\n\n**Caution**\nThis is reassuring, but not definitive. If the lesion is **changing, bleeding, itching, enlarging, or looks different from your other moles**, that would still raise concern.\n\n**Next step**\nI recommend running the **distillation tool** now so I can give you a **comprehensive medical report** of the whole conversation and the suggested next steps.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0fc6579adecff2a70169e8c85ae5f88191a7aad69ca760e211\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":205,"output":195,"cacheRead":46720,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47120,"cost":{"input":0.0005125,"output":0.002925,"cacheRead":0.01168,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.015117499999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776863321009,"responseId":"resp_0fc6579adecff2a70169e8c859872c8191808154db2fd842d7"}}
